I eat my dinner.
Then I sit on the sofa.
Now I am relaxing.
I take my mobile phone.
I video-call my home in Mexico.
My mother and father answer the phone.
"Hello, how are you both?" I ask them.
"We are fine, Maya," my mother says.
Then I see my younger sister, Sofia.
She is playing with our dog, Lola.
"Hi Sofia, what are you doing?" I ask.
"I am petting Lola," Sofia replies.
My parents ask about my daily routine.
"My routine is good," I tell them.
"I am learning new things at the office," I say.
"I go to the office by bus every day."
"The people here are very nice."
We chat for a long time.
Now I am feeling sleepy.
I say goodnight to everyone and go to bed.
